Vectezium is a modified version of Vector (https://github.com/vectordotdev/vector), forked from
Vector v0.60.0 (commit 0d0b35865036f8b5c2f0104d9744fa84985ffff1). The `vectezium` branch of
https://github.com/yokunade/Vectezium adds a shared change-data-capture core, the mysql_cdc and
postgres_cdc sources, and two azure_blob sink options. The demo builds it at the commit pinned in
vectezium/Dockerfile, which is the Source Code Form of the image it builds.

Modifications copyright (c) 2026 yokunade, licensed under the Mozilla Public License, version 2.0
(MPL-2.0), like Vector itself. A built image carries this licence, notice and the third-party
crate list in /usr/share/doc/vectezium/, with a link to the source.

The third-party Rust crates compiled into Vectezium, and their licences, are listed in the fork's
LICENSE-3rdparty.csv; LICENSE-3rdparty-cdc.csv lists the ones the CDC sources add.

